      en: "Nevado del Huila is the highest volcano in Colombia and the highest peak in the Central Cordillera, standing at 5,364 meters. It is a massive volcanic complex with several peaks and a large glacial area that feeds the Magdalena and Paez rivers. After centuries of dormancy, the volcano became significantly active again in 2007, causing major landslides and evacuations in the surrounding valleys. The area is also an important cultural site for the Nasa indigenous people, who have lived on its slopes for generations."
