      en: "The Puracé Volcano is an active stratovolcano located in the Central Cordillera near the historic city of Popayán. It is one of the most accessible volcanoes in Colombia, with a trail that leads hikers past smoking fumaroles and sulfurous vents to the edge of its massive crater. The surrounding Puracé National Park is a wonderland of volcanic activity, featuring hot springs, the spectacular Bedón waterfall, and the Valley of the Statues. It is also one of the few places in Colombia where you can reliably see the majestic Andean Condor in the wild."
