      en: "San Andrés is the largest island in a Caribbean archipelago located about 700 kilometers north of mainland Colombia, closer to Nicaragua than to the coast. It is famous for its Sea of Seven Colors, where the varying depths and coral reefs create a stunning palette of blues and turquoises. The island has a unique cultural identity, with a Raizal population that speaks San Andrés Creole, an English-based language. It is a major duty-free port and a popular tourist destination, offering world-class snorkeling, white sand beaches, and a vibrant Caribbean nightlife."
